Summary: Report network address changes on macOS
Category: system
Kind: fix
Origin: crossover
From: CrossOver 25.1.1
Source: https://media.codeweavers.com/pub/crossover/source/crossover-sources-25.1.1.tar.gz (sources/wine/dlls/nsiproxy.sys/{nsi.c,device.c})
Upstream: no
Why: Wine 10.0 only reports IP address changes through netlink on Linux; on macOS NotifyAddrChange/NotifyIpInterfaceChange never fire. Watch a PF_SYSTEM kernel event socket instead, and name nsiproxy's threads. CX's wow64 unix-call thunks for nsiproxy are not in 10.0_8 and are left out.
Evidence: Sikarugir 10.0_8: nsiproxy.so: 'PF_SYSTEM socket creation failed', 'SIOCSKEVFILT failed', 'error receiving, len %d'; nsiproxy.sys: UTF-16 wine_nsi_request, wine_nsi_notification; nsiproxy.so has no __wine_unix_call_wow64_funcs.
Applies to: wine 10.0

diff --git a/dlls/nsiproxy.sys/device.c b/dlls/nsiproxy.sys/device.c
index c64f61e..fe12ba6 100644
--- a/dlls/nsiproxy.sys/device.c
+++ b/dlls/nsiproxy.sys/device.c
@@ -457,6 +457,8 @@ static DWORD WINAPI request_thread_proc( void *arg )
 {
     LIST_ENTRY *entry;
 
+    SetThreadDescription( GetCurrentThread(), L"wine_nsi_request" );
+
     while (WaitForSingleObject( request_event, INFINITE ) == WAIT_OBJECT_0)
     {
         TRACE( "request_event triggered\n" );
@@ -486,6 +488,8 @@ static DWORD WINAPI notification_thread_proc( void *arg )
     LIST_ENTRY *entry, *next;
     NTSTATUS status;
 
+    SetThreadDescription( GetCurrentThread(), L"wine_nsi_notification" );
+
     while (!(status = nsiproxy_call( nsi_get_notification, &params )))
     {
         EnterCriticalSection( &nsiproxy_cs );
diff --git a/dlls/nsiproxy.sys/nsi.c b/dlls/nsiproxy.sys/nsi.c
